select left(r::text,600) x from (select engine_manual_apply(208,'ce61eb07272651948a2530b6a81a8a65',$p$[{"old": "To revise: call engine_manual_apply (ASK 421) in the same batch as SET LOCAL truth.session_id.", "new": "To revise: call engine_manual_apply (ASK 421) in the same batch as SET LOCAL truth.session_id and SET LOCAL truth.card = '<card label> <press time>Z <thread seat>' (ASK 477)."}, {"old": "EXECUTE is revoked from PUBLIC, anon and authenticated. Limit: an old text that overlaps itself is counted once.", "new": "EXECUTE is revoked from PUBLIC, anon and authenticated. Limit: an old text that overlaps itself is counted once.\n- Every insert forces an audit_log row (engine_manual_guard, AFTER INSERT): version, md5, length, and since ASK 477 card=<truth.card or NONE>, session=<truth.session_id or NONE> and from=v<prior version> hash=<prior md5 12>. It is record only: a write without truth.card still succeeds and is marked card=NONE. The card field is the writer's claim, not proof of a press; the press is the card in the writer's thread."}]$p$::jsonb,null,null,null,null,null,false) r) s;